{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018KDzv4frbuBk1aYVS9o4x5","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"response\":\"Here's the 5-day picture (Sat 17th through Wed 21st), with the weekend as the headline:\\n\\n| City | Sat 17 | Sun 18 | Rest of week | Picnic verdict |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| Delhi | 30/19°C, sunny | 31/18°C, clear, 0% rain | Sunny, dry all 5 days | **Winner** |\\n| Pune | 34/22°C, partly sunny, 5% rain | 33/22°C, partly sunny | Dry, 32-33°C | Solid runner-up |\\n| Mumbai | 34/26°C, sunny | 34/27°C, sunny | Sunny, 34-36°C | Dry but brutal: feels like 42-44°C |\\n| Kolkata | 33/25°C, light rain (55%) | 33/24°C, partly sunny | Clears to sunny | Skip Saturday, ok Sunday but sticky, feels like 38°C |\\n| Bengaluru | 28/21°C, light rain (44%) | 28/21°C, cloudy, 55% rain | Cloudy, 20-30% rain | Wet all weekend |\\n| Chennai | 32/25°C, heavy thunderstorms (75%) | 29/26°C, thunderstorms (40%) | Storms build, 65mm Wed | Avoid, storms all week |\\n\\n**Best picnic city: Delhi, and Sunday is the day.** Clear skies, zero rain chance, 31°C with feels-like only 32, comfortable 50% humidity, and a rare 18°C morning so you can picnic early without melting. The whole week is dry there too, so no risk of a weather scramble. Pune is the backup if you want cooler-ish coastal Deccan air, but it runs 4-5 degrees hotter with more haze. Bengaluru would usually be the mild pick, but it's in a rainy patch, and Chennai is getting hammered by thunderstorms through Wednesday.\\n\\nOne caution if Delhi wins: UV index is 6, so shade and sunscreen matter more than the thermometer suggests.\",\"status\":\"complete\",\"conversationId\":\"de6f6511-94f9-46b3-8008-1839d7302d88\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3cb5b31e-e8fc-4c6a-a39d-ff925f443785","uuid":"b11c1054-9684-442c-b371-d2fdc2a96b88","timestamp":"2026-10-17T10:54:56.046Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"response\":\"Here's the 5-day picture (Sat 17th through Wed 21st), with the we